  "conclusion": "R6 resolved (grounded SAR energy, 2.4): readout precision gates MC AND the readout DOMINATES RC energy -- the SAR comparator (= the EXTRACTED 48 fJ sky130 StrongARM SA) is 88-99% of total energy even at b=3, so reservoir_energy.py's 'free readout' is flat wrong. BUT because the comparator term is b-LINEAR (not 2^b), the resolution penalty is GENTLE: b=3 -> b=10 costs only 38x the energy for 3.66x the MC (vs the ~230x the crude 2^b model implied). => the real energy lever is NOT minimizing bits but AMORTIZING the comparator: column-shared SA + subsampled readout (M<N stays on the frontier); moderate-high res (b~8) is affordable. Design rule: bill the (dominant) shared-comparator readout and optimize by SHARING it across columns/nodes, not by going low-res. Honesty: mean-field MC; E_comp from extracted SA, E_capDAC/E_dev order-of-mag; claim is the frontier shape + the comparator-dominance, as ratios."
